course: dictionary
lesson: 13060
title: Joined together, but still themselves
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Federated means joined together in a group, but each part still keeps some of its own power or work. Think of a team of schools that share one head teacher while each school still has its own name and building.
explain: «Australia is a federation of states, and each state keeps some power of its own.» The states join under one central government, but they are not all squashed into one. The clue is the word «of» and the idea of keeping some power.
explain: «The two village schools are federated, so they share one head teacher and one governing body.» Federated schools are still separate schools, but they are joined up. Ask yourself: are the parts joined, and do they still keep something of their own? If yes, federated fits.
fact: Federated means joined together under one central body while keeping some power of their own.
fact: «Federated states» are states that have joined a bigger country but still make some of their own decisions.
fact: In England, «federated schools» share one governing body, and often one head teacher.
fact: In computing, a federated system shares the work between separate computers.
fact: The USA, Canada, Australia and Germany are federations of states or provinces.
exercise: «Australia is a federation of states, and each state keeps some power of its own.» What does federation mean here? | A kind of desert | *A group of states joined under one central government | A type of sports team | A single state with no others
exercise: «The two village schools are federated, so they share one head teacher.» What does federated mean here? | *Joined together and sharing one governing body | Closed down for good | Split up into unrelated schools | Painted in the same colours
exercise: In computing, what does a federated system do? | Stores one copy of every file on paper | Turns off when it is not used | Has only one computer in it | *Shares the work between separate computers
test: «Each state in a federated country keeps some power of its own.» What does keeps some power of its own suggest? | *They still make some of their own decisions | They are ruled by one leader only | They have no power at all | They must ask another country before they speak
test: Two schools that are federated share one what? | A library | *Governing body | A playground | A school bus
exam: Which word best describes a group of schools that share one governing body and often one head teacher? | Separate | *Federated | Ancient | Curt
